# Blinds panel

A full `blinds` tile is an edge-to-edge page of Home Assistant areas that have covers: room list on the left, covers of the chosen room on the right. Rows reuse the lights page's cover row (tilt slider + open/close switch). Alarm stays its own page; this is covers only.

## Wiring

- Catalogue kind `blinds` in `_kinds.yaml`: sizes `[full]`, card `none`, no entity.
- `OTHER_TILE_KINDS` / `OTHER_TILE_FULL_KINDS` include `blinds`. `kindSource('blinds')` opens a full page.
- `Tile.edgeToEdge()` and `Tiles.kt` dispatch to `blindsPanel`. `hasOwnTaps` includes `blinds`.
- Rooms: `LightsRoomsRepository.rooms(BLINDS_DOMAINS)` (`cover` only). Empty rooms are filtered out. Cached per domain set. Loaded into `RenderData.blindsRooms` when the screen has a blinds tile.
- UI state: `BlindsUiStore` / `RenderData.blindsUi` (chosen room). Verb `blinds_room` → `BlindsActions` → Rebuild.
- Cover taps go through catalogue verbs on `e:<entity>` (tilt, open_tilt, close_tilt, …).

## Room subtitle

Count of `cover.*` in the room that are `open`: `ui.blinds_one_open`, `ui.blinds_many_open`, `ui.blinds_all_closed`. Bound like lights-on counts.

## Editor

`GridMockup.vue` draws the same chrome as lights with title `BLINDS` and `blindsRoomRows` (`blindsOpenCount.ts`). `TileDrawer.vue` treats full blinds as edge-to-edge.

